{"availability":"available","full":"IdanShalem/react-broadcast-sync","name":"react-broadcast-sync","description":"Sync state and events across browser tabs in React - a lightweight, type-safe hook over the BroadcastChannel API","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":20,"forks":1,"created":"2025-05-06T18:08:38Z","updated":"2026-10-04T06:10:49Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://react-broadcast-sync-3w3m.vercel.app/","topics":[],"demo":"https://react-broadcast-sync-3w3m.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:41.959Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:41.959Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:41.959Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T06:11:41.959Z","stars":20,"forks":1}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Easily sync UI state or user events across browser tabs in React apps — notifications, presence, forms, and more. This package provides a clean and type-safe abstraction over the native API, enabling efficient, scoped, and reliable cross-tab messaging.","When to use it: React apps that need to share ephemeral state or events between browser tabs of the same origin (logout, notifications, presence, draft sync). It wraps the browser BroadcastChannel API in a hook (useBroadcastChannel) and an optional BroadcastProvider.","When not to use it: syncing to a server or other devices, persisting data across reloads (use localStorage/IndexedDB), or messaging across different origins."],"features":["Simple and intuitive API","Real-time synchronization across tabs","Automatic message expiration and cleanup","Send/receive any serializable message","Namespace and source scoping support"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/IdanShalem/react-broadcast-sync/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0dce8661850b39c1ebce0b2479e376e3b3ca0c5bf53e801210e8182e34473dba","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:42.095Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:11:42.095Z","projectInsights":{"v